        "name": "USN-4737-2",
        "description": "USN-4737-1 fixed a vulnerability in Bind. This update provides the corresponding update for Ubuntu 12.04 ESM and Ubuntu 14.04 ESM.  Original advisory details:   It was discovered that Bind incorrectly handled GSSAPI security policy  negotiation. A remote attacker could use this issue to cause Bind to crash,  resulting in a denial of service, or possibly execute arbitrary code. In  the default installation, attackers would be isolated by the Bind AppArmor  profile.",
        "aliases": [
          "CVE-2020-8625"
        ]
